extraction_notes: |
  Read from Rifts World Book 6: South America printed 134-135 (cache p135-p136),
  the text layer checked against a 150 dpi render of printed 134. Printed 133
  (cache p134) is the Chief Gatherer Kastor, an N.P.C., and was read for
  context only.

  1. NOT RECOMMENDED FOR PLAYERS, G.M.-ALLOWED. The book''s note says so; the
     class is transcribed in full and the warning leads the restrictions.
  2. XP_TABLE IS THE RACE''S OWN LADDER, "Cibola Pincer Warriors & Cibola
     Gatherers", in the experience tables (cache p169, printed 168 by the
     book''s +1 offset). Lower bounds stored as printed: 0, 2,141, 4,201 ...
     346,001. The pairing with the Pincer Warrior is the book''s.
  3. MDC_BASE is the carapace figure, 1D4x100+200. The S.D.C.-environment
     alternative (1D4x100+100 S.D.C., 1D6x10 H.P.) is a restriction line
     rather than sdc_base/hit_points_base, since storing both would give the
     sheet two pools the creature never has at once. No men_of_arms line: the
     class states mdc_base.
  4. P.P.E. is printed "3D6X10+P.E. attribute, plus 2D6 per level"; I.S.P.
     "M.E. attribute plus 2D4X10+30; add 3D6 I.S.P. per additional level" (the
     text layer reads "3D61.S.P."; the render shows 3D6 I.S.P.).
  5. PSIONICS: "any psionic category (including super)" is stored as the four
     core categories - Healing, Physical, Sensitive, Super. Mind Bleeder and
     Phase powers are other books'' closed disciplines and are not opened here.
     Type is master because Super is reachable.
  6. THE THREE BARRED POWERS are Mind Wipe, Psi-Sword and "possess other",
     matched to the catalog''s Mentally Possess Others. "Available after third
     level" is read as level 4 onward: the starting picks and the level 2 and 3
     grants exclude them, levels 4-15 are unrestricted.
  7. MAGIC: four spells from levels 1-4 at creation, then one per level capped
     at the character''s own level. General invocations only - no tradition.
  8. SKILLS. Dragonese/Elf at 98% is Language: Dragonese (a fixed figure).
     Track Animals is Track & Trap Animals, Track Humans is Tracking (people),
     Demon Lore is Lore: Demons & Monsters, D-Bee Lore is Lore: D-Bee. Each
     base is catalog base plus the printed bonus.
  9. THE EIGHT "OTHER" SKILLS are a choose-8 group in the R.C.C. skills with a
     +10% bonus, not occ_related_skills: the book prints them as part of the
     R.C.C. skill list and pairs the gatherer with no O.C.C. "Any category" is
     every Rifts skill category in the catalog; Horsemanship and Cowboy are
     left out as not Rifts-general.
  10. HAND TO HAND: the book grants no fighting style and prints no upgrade
      price, so no hand_to_hand block. Five attacks per melee is attacks_base.
  11. BONUSES are the R.C.C.''s printed ones (+2 strike, +3 parry and dodge, +1
      roll, +2 vs magic, +3 vs psionics). Kastor''s larger figures are an
      N.P.C.''s and were not used.
  12. EQUIPMENT: the book names no specific energy or techno-wizard weapon, so
      the choice lists are a catalog set; the trade items are value, not coin,
      and are a restriction line.
  13. Average Level of Experience 2D4+1 is an N.P.C. figure and is not stored.
